ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "5.0.5", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Buffs and debuffs: the |cffffffffBorder|r aura swipe draws a thicker ring around the icon, so the time left is easier to read. Thanks for the feedback!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Target and focus no longer fade when you stand right next to an enemy. Range fading checked the first rank of your spells, which the game stops counting once you learn a higher one: a warrior or rogue was left with only Charge or Throw, which can't reach up close. It now uses the best rank you know. Thanks to the players who reported it!" },
    { version = "5.0.4", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Forever and FlareUI styles: the |cffffffffrest, combat and threat glows|r now tint the portrait's own border with a soft pulse, instead of a bright line around it. Threat comes first while you have it.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Controllers: both analog sticks work again with FlareUI on. Since 5.0 the controller radial kept listening to the sticks all the time; now it only listens while it is open. Thanks to the player who reported it!" },
    { version = "5.0.3", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar|r has its own switch again, next to Main Frames. Turn it off and Blizzard's cast bar comes back (after a reload). Thanks to everyone who missed it!\n• Player frame, Edit Mode: |cffffffffStandalone Cast Bar|r is gone. The |cffffffffCast Bar|r section stays, for a cast bar on the player frame itself, now off by default and apart from the Player Cast Bar.\n• The settings window is a little taller, so the Unit Frames page fits without scrolling." },
    { version = "5.0.2", text = "|cffffd100New|r\n• |cffffffffItalian|r and |cffffffffLatin American Spanish|r, and a full |cffffffffSpanish (Spain)|r translation. Pick one in |cffffffffSettings → Language|r, or let FlareUI follow your game's language.\n• |cffffffffPortuguese (Brazil)|r is complete again, with shorter labels that fit the settings and the words players use: buffs, debuffs, pet, cast bar, frames.\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffSimplified Item Stats|r (off). Item tooltips say \"+12 Spell Power\" instead of \"Equip: Increases damage and healing done by magical spells and effects by up to 12.\", set bonuses too.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Item tooltips show stats as the game writes them again. The short form, always on since 5.0, is now the |cffffffffSimplified Item Stats|r switch under Tooltips. Thanks to everyone who asked!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: with a node-finding addon and Find Minerals or Find Herbs on, the coordinates, the header bar (tracking, zone, clock and calendar), the mail icon and the day/night badge no longer fly across the screen with your cursor or flicker. Thanks to the players who reported it!" },
    { version = "5.0.1", text = "|cffffd100New|r\n• |cffffffffVisibility is now a list of toggles|r on bars, the XP bar, buffs, debuffs, the quest tracker, the minimap, Resource Bars and the Fake Cooldown Manager. Tick |cffffffffIn Combat|r, |cffffffffHas a Target|r, |cffffffffHas an Attackable Target|r, |cffffffffIn a Group|r or |cffffffffNot Mounted|r in any mix: any one of them shows it. Your current choice carries over.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r (on). Blizzard's Cooldown Manager in FlareUI's look: its bars like FlareUI's cast bars, its buff icons like your FlareUI buffs. Everything it lets you set still works. Thanks to the player who asked!\n• Action Bars: the |cffffffffFlareUI XP Bar|r switch is back (on). Off brings back Blizzard's XP and reputation bars after a reload.\n• Player frame, Edit Mode: a |cffffffffCast Bar|r section, for a cast bar on the frame itself. *(Reworked in 5.0.3.)*\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Health, power and threat numbers show in full up to 9,999 (\"8742\", not \"8.7K\").\n• |cffffffffSettings read the same everywhere.|r Names are in Title Case, options are grouped the same way (dropdowns, then sliders, then switches) in the settings and in every Edit Mode dialog, and one thing has one name. The renames you may look for:\n      - |cffffffffVisibility|r (was Show Condition or Show) and |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r (was Min Alpha)\n      - |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffBuff Size|r, |cffffffffDebuff Size|r, |cffffffffGrowth|r, |cffffffffXP Text|r, |cffffffffThreat Text|r, |cffffffffSort By|r\n      - |cffffffffKeep Bar 1 in Stances|r, |cffffffffHide Bubbles in Instances|r, |cffffffffController Bar|r\n      - |cffffffffOff|r instead of None on Health Text, Power Text, Aura Swipe and Aura Timer\n\n  Searching an old name still finds the option.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffSteady attack highlight|r is gone. Attack, Auto Shot and Shoot blink as Blizzard's do." },
